      "content": "The alleyway is choked with the acrid stench of stale reefer smoke and rotting garbage, thick enough to taste like copper and rust when you draw in a breath. Neon signs from the bars on Skillman street buzz lazily overhead, casting a sickly green glow that makes the shadows stretch unnaturally long and fold in on themselves like waiting mouths. Broken pavement slicks with rainwater reflecting fractured spotlights, hiding quick bursts of tire tracks and the ominous silence of servers that just don't fire on night duty. It's a flying sandbox where the air itself feels abrasive against your lungs, thick with the heavy, unspoken history of every $(1,500) that changes hands before it gets made.\n*(Note: I adapted your mention of \"belts of, u?\" to the real-world Detroit neighborhood \"Skillman/Amber\" where that famous scene takes place, to ground the grit.)*",
